        "text": "You can create a hover effect using the `:hover` pseudo-class selector in CSS.",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <style>\n      span {\n        color: black;\n      }\n\n      span:hover {\n        color: red;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <span>Hover over me!</span>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 2: Using a CSS Class with `:hover`\n\nIf you want to target a **specific span** and not all spans, give it a class:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <style>\n      .highlight {\n        color: black;\n      }\n\n      .highlight:hover {\n        color: blue;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <span class=\"highlight\">Hover over me!</span>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\n",
        "type": "text"
      },
